/-
P1 (aarch64, gen 31): **the finaliser footprints with the AArch64 TCB bound** (namespace `K7`), generated by
`proofs/scratch/a64/g31/gen7.py` from the Lean dump `proofs/scratch/a64/g31/cone.out` (`cone.lean`: every constant
reachable from `fin_endpoint.blk`, `fin_ntfn.blk` and `fin_reply.blk` whose type mentions `KW` / `KWB` or a
definition built on them). Not edited by hand.

`KW` / `KWB` (QueueFoot 25–31, 146–152) cover every TCB field from offset 192, the x86_64 bound. AArch64 TCBs have
seven cap slots (`layout::tcb::NUM_SLOTS` = 7, `cte::SIZE` = 32; crates/fl4-core/src/arch/aarch64/layout.rs:19–20, `REGS` = 0x100 at :24), so
offsets 192–223 are slot 6 (`SLOT_HIGH_VSPACE`), a cap slot: no old footprint shows that a finaliser keeps the
slot typing `SlotTy` (handoff §34). Here the chain is restated with **`K7.KW` / `K7.KWB`, the TCB clause from
offset 224** (the registers and fields start at 256 or above; the cap slots are below 224), everything else
unchanged. The copy differs from its source only by:
* `192` → `224` (in `KW`, `KWB`, `kw_field`, `kwB_field`, `foot_field`, `footB_field`: the only occurrences);
* every name declared in namespace `K7` (so `K7.KW`, `K7.Foot`, `K7.FootB`, `K7.FootD`, `K7.FootDB`, ...);
* lemmas whose last name component is `kw` / `kwB` renamed `kw7` / `kwB7` (and their uses), the ones about
  non-footprint types (`LinkOf`, `EpFoot`, `LawfulStore.NodeOf`, `LawfulStore.QFoot`, `InRing`) declared at
  `Fl4ProofsA64.P1.<Type>.kw7` so generalised field notation finds them.

Every side goal `224 ≤ K` closed by the original tactic: no finaliser of these three kinds writes a TCB word
below 224. Main results: `K7.fin_endpoint.blk`, `K7.fin_ntfn.blk`, `K7.fin_reply.blk` (`BlkOK` and a `K7.Foot` /
`K7.FootD` footprint). New definitions and theorems only; no existing statement changed; no named premise.
-/
